---
title: Crunchy Chicken Salad
author: Mildred McKinzie
category: Salads
source: Loving Memories of Mildred
---

@chopped peanuts{1/2%c}
@cubed, cooked chicken{2%c}
@finely chopped onions{1/4%c}
@mayonnaise{2/3%c}
@sesame seeds{1/2%c}
@soy sauce{2%Tbsp}
@red wine{2%Tbsp}

Spread peanuts and sesame seeds in shallow pan. Toast in 350 degree oven for 8 to 10 minutes, stirring often. When cooled, combine with chicken and chopped onion. In a separate bowl, blend soy sauce, wine and mayonnaise. Add to chicken mixture, tossing thoroughly. Chill.
